\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 31/09/89\ \ \ \ \ author: Elly van Munster\\
Attribute 'contraction' for PREP introduced (instead of specifying the key of 
the PREP). Now the rule is valid not only for 'de' and 'a', but also for idiom
prepositions ending on 'de' or 'a' (e.g. detr\'{a}s de, respecto a, etc..)
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
